The idea is not bad, but you've got a problem. Either object creation is
randomized, so if you really *need* a special item and you only have, say,
5 levels to find it, the chance to actually get lucky is pretty low.
Another way would be to make it guaranteed but you have to find it, so you
would know where to get it, and Hunt-the-special-item-only-needed-for-Gehennom
doesn't sound that exciting. Or you could add a tough monster that guards the
special something, but I'm afraid that wouldn't be much different from 
getting the Candelabrum. I like the idea of adding Charon and Cerberus (both 
are in the code but commented out), so maybe one could make them more than
Yet Another Monster (tm).

Intrinsicwise... in mythology heroes going into the underworld had to face
hard restrictions, like not looking back (okay, maybe I'm mixing something
up), and not answering to the spirits calling. Some kind of challenge like 
this would be nice. Other ideas have been preventing food generation, 
have Hell be filled with genocided monsters, maybe HP would regenerate much
slower. I don't know, I'm not feeling extremely creative.

